+# PPTX Engine v5 — Version History (archive)
+
+This file archives detailed version notes for the PPTX engine v5 (`supabase/functions/export-pptx-v4`).
+The current version + active architecture lives in `replit.md`. Older entries are kept here for context
+when investigating regressions or understanding why specific guards / repairs exist.
+
+- **v5.5.8** — **Code synthesis priority inversion** (stop demoting code slides, start completing them). User report: v5.5.5-v5.5.7 silently converted CODE slides to bullets/concepts whenever repair failed (slide 14 perdeu snippet, slide 20 virou bullets, módulo 7 perdeu unittest/logging/pdb). Fix is architectural: synthesize a minimal complete example from module context BEFORE demoting; demote only as last resort with explicit `[CODE-SLIDE-CONVERSION]` log. (1) **`synthesizeMinimalCompleteExample(moduleKind, ctx, slideTitle)`** new function (~115 lines) returns `{code, source}` or `null`. Per-kind canonical snippets: `oop` (reuses `ctx.classes[0]`+`ctx.vars[0]`+first non-`__init__` method when available, else canonical `Carro` class with `exibir_info()`); `tests_logs` (title-routed to `pdb.set_trace`/`logging.basicConfig+info+warning`/`unittest.TestCase` with `assertEqual`); `json_apis` (`requests.get`+`status_code==200`+`response.json()`); `files_exceptions` (`with open` + `try/except FileNotFoundError`); `control_flow` (`if/elif/else` `classificar(nota)`); `data_structures` (list of dicts + `sum(p["preco"] for p in ...)`); `fundamentals` (`input()`+`print(f"...")`); `best_practices` (typed function with docstring). Source label `module_ctx` when reusing accumulator symbols, `canonical_<kind>` for fallback. (2) **Guardrail 2 INVERTED**: `layout=code` with empty code → call `synthesizeMinimalCompleteExample(moduleKind, prevSymbols, out.title)` FIRST. If success → assign synth code + `[CODE-SYNTHESIS] reason=empty_code beforeLines=0 afterLines=N source=…`. Only if `null` → emit `[CODE-SLIDE-CONVERSION] from=CODE to=CONCEPT reason=empty_code_no_synth_available` THEN demote. (3) **Guardrail 4 INVERTED**: when `repairIncompleteCodeExample` returns `null` AND layout=code → try synth; on success replace code + log `[CODE-SYNTHESIS] reason=repair_failed (<reason>)`. Only if synth also `null` → `[CODE-SLIDE-CONVERSION]` + demote. (4) **Guardrail 5 INVERTED**: code-slide integrity fail (codeLines<3 or no syntax) → try synth before demote. (5) **Logs added**: `[CODE-SYNTHESIS]` (success path with `beforeLines`/`afterLines`/`source`/`moduleKind`), `[CODE-SLIDE-CONVERSION]` (failure path with `from=CODE to=CONCEPT reason=…`). User-spec compliance: every CODE→CONCEPT transition is now logged with explicit reason — no more silent demotes. **Constraint preserved**: `repairIncompleteCodeExample` still runs first (fast path); synth is the second-chance layer. Renderer/planner/preservation/qaVeto/billing/route/schema unchanged. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.8"`.
+- **v5.5.7** — **Editorial polish #2** (json/api objectives, ellipsis-block, print-inst→method). All in `index.ts` + 1 line in `presentation-plan.ts`. (1) **`py_json_api` key added to `PYTHON_OBJECTIVE_TAILS`** with 5 concrete tails (Interpretar JSON / Serializar com json.dumps()-loads() / Realizar requests.get()-post() / Validar response.status_code / Converter response.json() para dicts). (2) **`detectModuleDomainPython` JSON/API branch** added BEFORE `py_files` so "Trabalhando com JSON e APIs Web" titles route to `py_json_api` instead of `py_files`/`py_generic`. Pattern: `/\bjson\b|\bapis?\b|\brest\b|\bhttp\b|\brequests\b/`. (3) **`[OBJECTIVE-JSON-API-REPAIR]` dedicated log** in `repairLearningObjective` when sub==="py_json_api" — fires alongside the generic `[V5-OBJECTIVE-REPAIR]` so prod filters can isolate the slide-28 class regression. (4) **`[CODE-ELLIPSIS-BLOCK]` log** at top of `repairIncompleteCodeExample`: when `validateSemanticCodeCompleteness(before)` returns `ellipsis_*` or `todo_*`, emit `[CODE-ELLIPSIS-BLOCK] slide=N reason=… action=attempt_repair` BEFORE the repair attempt — guarantees per-spec observability that no `# ...` slipped through silently. (5) **`print(<inst>) → <inst>.<method>()` repair pattern** in `repairIncompleteCodeExample`: detects a bare `print(meu_carro)` line where `meu_carro` was assigned `ClassName(...)` AND `moduleCtx.funcs` has a non-`__init__`/`init`/`main` method → rewrite to `meu_carro.exibir_info()` (uses first valid method from module context). Logs `[CODE-REPAIR] pattern=print_inst_to_method inst=… method=…`. Fixes user-reported POO regression where slide ended in `print(carro)` + `# ...`. (6) **Mirror update in `presentation-plan.ts`**: `json_apis` tails grow 3→5 entries with the same concrete strings (planner-side `repairPlan` now substitutes the right vocabulary at the source). `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.7"`. No renderer/planner-architecture/preservation/qaVeto/billing/route/schema changes.
+- **v5.5.6** — **Context-aware code repair (Manus-inspired flow)**. v5.5.5 saw repair work but in isolation: a slide could be "completed" with names disconnected from the module's earlier vocabulary. Three additions: (1) **`CodeSymbols` type widened** to `{classes, vars, funcs, imports}` (was `{classes, vars}`); `extractCodeSymbols` now also captures `def funcname(` and `from X import` / `import X`. (2) **`extractSemanticCodeContext(slides[])`** walks an array of accepted slides and returns the deduplicated UNION of all symbols across them — preserving order so `vars[i]` corresponds to `classes[i]` when both came from the same line (`livro = Livro("Python")` → classes[0]="Livro", vars[0]="livro"). (3) **Module accumulator wired in dedup loop**: `moduleCtx` replaces single-slide `prevSymbols`. After each kept slide → `moduleCtx = extractSemanticCodeContext(kept)`. So slide 5's repair sees ALL classes/vars introduced in slides 1-4 of the same module, not just slide 4. (4) **Drift guard inside `repairIncompleteCodeExample`**: when a slide defines `class X` AND `moduleCtx.classes` is non-empty AND `X` is NOT in `moduleCtx.classes` → refuse repair entirely (`return null`) and log `[CODE-CONTEXT-DRIFT] reason="class 'X' is new vs module context [Livro, ...]" action=refuse_repair`. Let Guardrail 4 demote layout=code to bullets — better than baking in a contradicting domain. (5) **Instance reuse from context**: when class IS in moduleCtx, repair looks up `moduleCtx.vars[ctxInstIdx]` to get the original instance name (e.g. `livro`) rather than synthesizing `cls.toLowerCase()`. So slide N+1 completing `class Livro` reuses `livro` from slide N. (6) **`[CODE-CONTEXT]` log on every successful class-demo repair**: `slide=N reusedClasses=["Livro"] reusedVariables=["livro"] newSymbols=[] contextualConsistency=PASSED`. `applyFinalGuardrails` signature now takes `prevSymbols: CodeSymbols` (was the narrow 2-field shape). No renderer / planner / preservation / qaVeto / billing / route / schema changes. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.6"`.
+- **v5.5.5** — Editorial-quality pass after v5.5.4 cleared the regression. User report: slides 13/37 still ended in `# ...`, slide 42 logging code never emitted, slide 18-20 mixed bullets+pseudo-code, slides 36/44/50 still had weak "(II)" content, slide 28 still showed "Compreender trabalhando..." JSON objective. Six additions, all in `applyFinalGuardrails` + dedup loop + `isGenericObjective`, no renderer/planner/preservation/qaVeto/billing/route changes. (1) **`extractCodeSymbols(code)`** returns `{classes, vars}` from a slide's code so the next slide's repair can reuse the same names. Wired in dedup loop: `prevSymbols = extractCodeSymbols(s.code)` after each kept slide. (2) **`validateSemanticCodeCompleteness(code)`** returns null when complete, else short reason: `empty`/`ellipsis_placeholder`/`ellipsis_comment_placeholder`/`todo_placeholder`/`too_few_code_lines`/`trailing_open_bracket`/`class_defined_but_unused`. Detects `# ...`/`// ...`/`...`/`# TODO`/`# continua`/`# restante omitido` anywhere; class with `__init__` but no instantiation/method-with-output; trailing `,:({[`; <2 real (non-comment) code lines. (3) **`repairIncompleteCodeExample(code, moduleKind, prevSymbols, slideNum)`** — best-effort completion. Patterns: `class_defined_but_unused` → append synthetic `def exibir(self): print(self.<attr>)` + `<inst> = <Class>(<args>)` + `<inst>.exibir()`, with `<inst>` reusing `prevSymbols.vars[0]` if the same class was defined in previous slide; `try` without `except` → append `except Exception as e: print(f"Erro: {e}")`; module=json_apis with `requests.get()` but no `.json()` → append `print(resp.json())`; module=tests_logs with `import logging` but no `logging.info/etc` → append `logging.info("Operação concluída")`. Returns null if no pattern fits. Logs `[CODE-REPAIR] slide=N pattern=… cls=…`. (4) **Guardrail 4 in `applyFinalGuardrails`**: runs `validateSemanticCodeCompleteness` after dangling repair; if reason!=null calls `repairIncompleteCodeExample`; if repair returns null AND `layout=code` → demote to bullets + clear code field (better empty bullets than rendered "# ..."). Logs `[CODE-COMPLETE] status=PASSED|PARTIAL|FAILED`. (5) **Guardrail 5 — code-slide integrity**: after Guardrail 4, if `layout=code` AND (`<3 real code lines` OR no syntax markers) → demote to bullets. Logs `[CODE-SLIDE-INTEGRITY] valid=false codeLines=N hasSyntax=…`. (6) **Weak-continuation detector** in dedup loop: title matching `/\((II|III|IV|V)\)$|parte [2-9]|continuação|parte ii+/i` checked against ALL previous slides in the module (not just immediate); if any jaccard ≥0.45 → DROP. Logs `[WEAK-CONTINUATION] slide=… similarity=… action=drop`. New aggregate counter `weak_continuation_dropped` in `[V5-GUARDRAILS]`. (7) **`isGenericObjective` looser pattern** in presentation-plan.ts: ANY of `compreender|entender|aplicar|identificar|conhecer|estudar|aprender|explorar|analisar|examinar` followed by gerund glue (`trabalhando|estudando|explorando|lidando|atuando|operando`) + `com|em|sobre` is generic regardless of suffix match. Catches slide 28 "Compreender trabalhando com JSON…" even when module title doesn't lexically match. `applyFinalGuardrails` signature now `(s, slideNum, moduleKind=null, prevSymbols={classes:[],vars:[]})`. `getModuleRule(courseTitle, moduleTitlesArr[mi])?.kind` resolved once per module. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.5"`.
+- **v5.5.4** — Four additions in response to Python deck regression after v5.5.3 (slides 15/34/38/42 + módulos 7/8 redundantes). (1) **`isCodeFragmentBullet()`** detects bullet items that leaked from code field — patterns: f-string interior (`{var['key']`), `f"...{`, format spec `:.2f")`, ends in `}")`/`)"`/`)"`, bare Python statement starters (`print(|return |def |class |if |for |while `), shell prompts (`>>>`/`$ `), comment leads (`#`). Wired as **Guardrail 1b** in `applyFinalGuardrails` BEFORE the layout-demote check so an items-only-of-code-fragments slide becomes empty and gets demoted. Logs `[CODE-BULLET-DROP]`. (2) **`stripTrailingPlaceholderComment()`** — Guardrail 1c — removes trailing `# ...`, `// ...`, `-- ...`, `# TODO`, `# FIXME`, `# continuar`, `# placeholder`, `# completar` lines from `out.code`. Walks backwards line-by-line so multi-line trailing placeholders are all stripped. Logs `[CODE-PLACEHOLDER-STRIP]`. (3) **Adjacent dedup now DROPS** instead of just relabeling when title matches AND items jaccard ≥0.6 (top 3 items, words >4 chars). Fixes módulos 7/8 "parte II" redundancy where v5.5.2 just appended " (II)" to genuine duplicates. New log `[TITLE-DEDUP-DROP]` + aggregate counter `adjacent_dropped` in `[V5-GUARDRAILS]`. Threshold 0.6 chosen to be conservative — slight content variation still gets the (II) suffix. (4) **`[PPTX][DIAG-FINAL]` mandatory log** at every Response site (success + 422 veto): `engine_version=X.Y.Z cache=miss fallback_used=false accepted_modules=[...] fallback_modules=[...] slide_count=N qa_status=... dedup_dropped=K status=exported|blocked`. Response JSON now also exposes `accepted_modules` + `fallback_modules` arrays so frontend can confirm engine path without parsing logs. New helper var `acceptedModuleNumbers` derived from `fallbackModuleNumbers`. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.4"`.
+- **v5.5.3** — **Module isolation reinforced after Python deck regression** (slides 34/35/37/38 of module 6 POO showed variáveis/operadores/input-print contamination). Three additions: (1) **`isBareFundamentalsTitleInAdvancedModule()` + validation 7d (FATAL)** — `BARE_FUNDAMENTALS_TITLE_RE` matches short generic titles like "Variáveis", "Operadores", "Tipos de Dados", "Hello World", "Entrada e Saída", "Input() e print()", "Atribuição" when they appear inside advanced modules (matched by `ADVANCED_MODULE_TITLE_RE`). `FUNDAMENTALS_TOPIC_RE` requires a qualifier ("básicas"/"primitivas"/"e tipos") so bare titles slipped through. New check fires FATAL → planner module rejected → legacy fallback. (2) **OOP positivity gate** — `computeOopPositivityFraction()` counts slides referencing OOP keywords (`class\b|classe|objeto|método|atributo|instância|herança|encapsulamento|polimorfismo|self\b|__init__|super()`). When `getModuleRule(...)?.kind === "oop"` and fraction <30% → `oopPositivityFail = true` → forced legacy fallback. Logs `[MODULE-PLANNER] module=N OOP positivity check FAILED: X% slides mention OOP keywords (need ≥30%) → forcing legacy fallback`. (3) **`repairOrphanPrepositions()`** — collapses duplicated/orphan prepositions like "dos de Python" → "de Python" (catches user-reported "Principais Aprendizados dos de Python" residue from cascading sanitizers). Helper exists; not yet wired into a specific call site (await user confirmation before applying to title sanitizer to avoid over-aggressive collapse). New imports in index.ts: `getModuleRule`, `computeOopPositivityFraction`. Per-module gate now: `inRange && !hasFatal && !hasBlocker && !oopPositivityFail`. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.3"`.
+- **v5.5.2** — Three additions to the final-guardrails pass: (1) **`repairDanglingAssignment` now correctly handles reassignment**: dropped the `before` check from `usedElsewhere` so `desconto = bruto * 0.05; desconto = bruto * 0.10` (slide 14) is recognized as dangling — only `after` matters because reassignment is shadowing, not "use". (2) **Pattern B: function-defined-but-never-called** — when last meaningful line is `return <expr>` or `pass`, walk backwards to find enclosing `def funcname(args)` (module-level only); if `funcname(` never appears outside the def body, append `print(funcname(<placeholders>))` with arg-name-aware defaults (numeric→0, string-ish→"x", else None). Fixes slide 47 ending in `return 0.0`. Logs `[CODE-COMPLETE-REPAIR] pattern=def_without_call`. (3) **Adjacent duplicate-title dedup** — `normalizeTitleForCompare()` (lowercase + strip punct/space) compares each slide title to the previous one in the SAME module; on match, appends roman-numeral suffix " (II)", " (III)" etc. Fixes slides 40/41 user report (both "Depurando Código com pdb"). Doesn't drop slides — content may differ; TOC needs unique titles. Aggregate log: `[V5-GUARDRAILS] applied to N slides | adjacent_title_dedup=K`. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.2"`.
+- **v5.5.1** — **Final-guardrails pass** to catch three classes of damage that bypass earlier layers because they're introduced by template splits / legacy chunks / direct planner emissions that don't go through `cleanSlideTitle`. New helper `applyFinalGuardrails(slide, slideNum)` runs ONCE per slide just after `[V5-QA-POSTREPAIR]` and just before render, with three checks: (1) **bare "Que X?" title rewrite** — `rewriteBareQueTitle()` catches titles like "Que boas práticas e organização de projetos?" (slide 45, user report) that escaped `polishEditorialTitle` because they came in via `processBatch` template-split (index.ts:3831/3841) or chunked `splitToBullets` (2922/2930) instead of slide intake; output: "Por que boas práticas e organização de projetos?"; conservative — no verb conjugation, just prefix "Por que " + lowercase first letter + ensure "?" suffix. (2) **layout="code" without code → demote to "bullets"** — fixes slide 49 ("Empacotando seu Projeto Python") that rendered as code template but had only bullet content; logs `[LAYOUT-DEMOTE] reason=empty_code`. (3) **dangling assignment in code → append print(var)** — `repairDanglingAssignment()` walks code backwards to last non-blank non-comment line, matches `varname = expression`, checks bracket balance + whether varname is used elsewhere or has print/return after; if dangling (slides 14/18 user report — `desconto = totalbruto * 0.05` ending), appends `<indent>print(<varname>)` so snippet ends with a complete, meaningful statement. Logs: `[TITLE-POLISH-FINAL]`, `[LAYOUT-DEMOTE]`, `[CODE-COMPLETE-REPAIR]`, aggregate `[V5-GUARDRAILS] applied to N slides`. Architecture untouched — strictly additive pass on `allModuleSlides` matrix between `tlog("post_repair_re_QA_done")` and the render loop. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.1"`.
+- **v5.5.0** — **Editorial polish layer**: new module `editorial-normalization.ts` with `polishEditorialTitle()` and `polishEditorialText()`. Title polish converts "Que <verb> X?" → "Por que <infinitive> x?" (e.g. "Que Representamos Dados?" → "Por que representar dados?"); preserves good titles ("O que é POO?", "Como Declarar Variáveis", "Tomada de Decisão com if, elif e else"). Text polish detects "shout mode" (>60% uppercase, length ≥12, not code) and sentence-cases the string while preserving: technical-preservation tokens (full pipeline: protect → polish → restore → integrity-check), HTTP/REST/JSON/SQL/HTML/CSS/URL acronyms, HTTP verbs (GET/POST/…), Python log levels (DEBUG/INFO/WARNING/ERROR/CRITICAL), PEP 8, dotted calls (`requests.get()`, `pdb.set_trace()`), backticked code, filenames (`app.py`), URLs. Wired in `cleanSlideTitle` + `cleanTakeawayTitle` (after structural normalisation) and on every item at both slide intake sites (index.ts:2848 + 7836). Logs: `[TITLE-POLISH] before=… after=…`, `[CASE-NORMALIZE] field=item before=… after=…`. Smoke tests at `__tests__/editorial.smoke.ts` cover all 5 user spec cases. Architecture untouched: planner / per-module gate / Technical Preservation Layer / qaVeto / fallback v3 / billing / routes / schema unchanged. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.5.0"`.
+- **v5.4.9** — **Two converging fixes for label-as-headline regression in slides 45/46 of the Python deck**. After v5.4.8 fixed the renderCards split, the user reported the same symptom (sentence promoted to bold uppercase headline) reappearing on diagram-layout slides ("Sistema de Logs com logging", "Depuração de Código com pdb"). Forensics: (1) **renderDiagram regression caused by my own v5.4.8 fix** — when `parseCardItem` rejected the colon-split, I had returned `{label: p.body.trim(), body: ""}` which dumped the entire sentence into the label slot. The diagram renderer (line ~2555) then ran `san(label).toUpperCase()` on it, producing a 30+ char uppercase bold band like "USE LOGGING PARA REGISTRAR EVENTOS DO SISTEMA" inside each step box. Fix: rejected split now returns `{label: \`Etapa ${i+1}\`, body: <full sentence>}` — synthetic short label per user spec, full sentence preserved in body region rendered in normal case. (2) **Slide-level `label` field accepted any string from planner** — sites at index.ts:2811 (slide intake) and :7795 (planner-binding rebuild) both did `String(s.label || "CONTEÚDO").slice(0, 32).toUpperCase()` with NO content validation. If planner emitted a sentence as `label` (e.g. derived from intent description), it became the uppercase section badge above the slide title via `header()`. Added `normalizeSlideLabel(rawLabel, defaultLabel, ctx)` helper that rejects labels >25 chars, >4 words, ending in stop-word, or containing conjugated verb (reuses PARSE_STOP_TAIL_RE / PARSE_VERB_3P_RE from v5.4.8); rejected labels fall back to `defaultLabel`. Applied at both intake sites. Logs each decision via `[LAYOUT-REGION-DEBUG] field=slide_label accepted=…`. `ENGINE_VERSION = "5.4.9"`. **renderTimeline / renderProcess confirmed innocent** — neither splits items nor uppercases item text; renderTimeline renders full sentences as body cards with normal case, renderProcess shows step text inside boxes with normal case. The architecture/planner/preservation-layer remain untouched.
